# SuperMemory – .gitignore
# Ship the skeleton (folders, _EXAMPLE_* files, templates).
# Keep all real user data out of version control.

# ── Obsidian internals ──────────────────────────────────
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/graph.json
.obsidian/cache/
.obsidian/community-plugins.json
.obsidian/plugins/

# ── Supervertaler/Workbench edit-metadata sidecars ──────
*.edtz

# ── User data: everything that is NOT an example or template ──
# Deny-all per content folder, then re-admit only _EXAMPLE_* files.
#
# This deliberately ignores EVERY file, not just *.md. The earlier
# ".md"-only rules let anything with a suffix after the extension slip
# through as untracked – e.g. files written as
# "Audit & Financial Reporting.md (frontmatter only)" – which a stray
# `git add -A` would then have committed to this PUBLIC repo. Deny-all
# closes that whole class rather than chasing individual patterns.
00_INBOX/*
!00_INBOX/_EXAMPLE_*.md
00_INBOX/_archive/

01_CLIENTS/*
!01_CLIENTS/_EXAMPLE_*.md

02_TERMINOLOGY/*
!02_TERMINOLOGY/_EXAMPLE_*.md

03_DOMAINS/*
!03_DOMAINS/_EXAMPLE_*.md

04_STYLE/*
!04_STYLE/_EXAMPLE_*.md

05_INDICES/*
!05_INDICES/_EXAMPLE_*.md

# Templates are always shipped — do NOT ignore 06_TEMPLATES/

# ── Common sensitive / binary files ─────────────────────
*.pdf
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.xliff
*.sdlxliff
*.sdlppx
*.sdlrpx
*.mqxliff
*.tmx
*.tbx
*.sdltb
*.zip
*.7z
*.tar.gz

# ── OS junk ─────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
